---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LightLine from '../components/LightLine.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const aboutOrigin = (Astro.site || new URL(SITE.url)).toString().replace(/\/$/, '');
const aboutUrl = `${aboutOrigin}/about/`;
const aboutSchema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'AboutPage',
    '@id': `${aboutUrl}#about`,
    name: `About ${SITE.name}`,
    description: SITE.mission,
    url: aboutUrl,
    inLanguage: SITE.language,
    isPartOf: { '@id': `${aboutOrigin}/#website` },
    mainEntity: {
      '@type': 'Person',
      '@id': `${aboutOrigin}/about/#ellis-graham`,
      name: SITE.teacher.name,
      jobTitle: SITE.teacher.role,
      description: SITE.teacher.shortBio,
      url: aboutUrl,
      image: {
        '@type': 'ImageObject',
        url: `${aboutOrigin}${SITE.teacher.image}`,
        width: SITE.teacher.imageWidth,
        height: SITE.teacher.imageHeight,
        caption: SITE.teacher.imageAlt,
      },
      worksFor: { '@id': `${aboutOrigin}/#organization` },
    },
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: `${aboutOrigin}/` },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: aboutUrl },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About ${SITE.name} — Mission & Bible Teaching`}
  description="Learn why Live In Jesus Name exists, who writes and edits our Scripture-anchored teachings, and how every article is built."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  jsonLd={aboutSchema}
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="reading-container">
      <p class="meta-caps" style="color: var(--gold-text); margin: 0 0 0.45rem 0;">
        About the Publication
      </p>
      <h1>A Quiet Room Where Scripture Speaks Plainly</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-soft);">
        <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is an independent Christian teaching publication built to help believers move
        from familiar Bible phrases into clear spiritual understanding, settled identity in Christ, and faithful everyday conduct.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <LightLine />

  <article class="reading-container article-prose" style="padding-block: 3rem;">
    <figure style="margin: 0 0 2.5rem 0;">
      <picture>
        <source
          type="image/avif"
          srcset="/images/open-scripture-720.avif 720w, /images/open-scripture-1200.avif 1200w"
          sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 680px"
        />
        <source
          type="image/webp"
          srcset="/images/open-scripture-720.webp 720w, /images/open-scripture-1200.webp 1200w"
          sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 680px"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/open-scripture-1200.webp"
          alt="An open clothbound Bible resting on a quiet wooden desk in morning light"
          width="1200"
          height="655"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
          style="border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);"
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="meta-caps" style="margin-top: 0.65rem;">
        Every teaching begins with the open text in context — never with hype or borrowed clichés.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>Why Live In Jesus Name Exists</h2>
    <p>
      Across the modern church, believers do not suffer from a shortage of religious noise; they suffer from a shortage of
      unhurried biblical clarity. Many love Jesus sincerely yet still carry quiet confusion about what happened at the New Birth,
      how grace and holiness fit together, and what it means to pray and live in Jesus’ Name between Sunday mornings.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> was founded to serve that exact need. Rather than publishing breathless commentary on passing controversies,
      we publish structured, long-form Scripture teachings organized into twelve monthly arcs across a 365-topic curriculum —
      so any reader, anywhere in the world, can study the New Testament’s core doctrines cleanly and systematically at no cost.
    </p>

    <h2>Who Teaches Here</h2>
    <figure class="author-portrait">
      <picture>
        <source
          type="image/webp"
          srcset="/images/author-ellis-graham-400.webp 400w, /images/author-ellis-graham-800.webp 800w"
          sizes="(max-width: 560px) 80vw, 340px"
        />
        <img
          src="/images/author-ellis-graham-400.jpg"
          srcset="/images/author-ellis-graham-400.jpg 400w, /images/author-ellis-graham-800.jpg 800w"
          sizes="(max-width: 560px) 80vw, 340px"
          alt={SITE.teacher.imageAlt}
          width="800"
          height="1067"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption class="meta-caps">{SITE.teacher.name} &middot; {SITE.teacher.role}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>
      Our studies are written and edited under the oversight of <strong>{SITE.teacher.name}</strong>, {SITE.teacher.role}.
      {SITE.name} is an original editorial teaching desk: we do not impersonate any living preacher or ministry, nor do we reprint
      or paraphrase third-party devotionals. Every exposition, illustration, weekday application, and closing confession is written
      fresh from the biblical text.
    </p>

    <h2>How Every Teaching Is Built</h2>
    <p>
      Every article on this site must satisfy an eighteen-point editorial audit before publication and follows an eight-step
      Scripture chain:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Anchor in the written text:</strong> Open with a full Scripture quotation and labeled translation.</li>
      <li><strong>Examine key words:</strong> Define biblical vocabulary plainly on first use without hiding behind jargon.</li>
      <li><strong>Confirm across books:</strong> Establish every central claim from at least three cross-references across Scripture.</li>
      <li><strong>Contrast truth and misconception:</strong> Distinguish gospel reality from both legalism and carelessness.</li>
      <li><strong>Bridge with everyday life:</strong> Illustrate spiritual principles clearly, then explain the principle directly.</li>
      <li><strong>Translate into Monday morning:</strong> Show what the doctrine looks like in speech, family, work, integrity, and stewardship.</li>
      <li><strong>Honour responsible wisdom:</strong> Affirm plainly that biblical faith works alongside diligence, honesty, and sound medical or professional care.</li>
      <li><strong>Respond in faith:</strong> Close with a Scripture-anchored confession and passages for personal verification, like the Bereans in Acts 17:11.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Our Commitment to Doctrinal Honesty</h2>
    <p>
      Where godly, Bible-honouring Christians have historically read a difficult verse with different nuances, we state our conviction
      clearly while acknowledging the conversation respectfully — without caricaturing fellow believers and without making reckless
      personal outcome guarantees that Scripture itself does not make.
    </p>
    <p>
      To read the ten foundational doctrines that govern every page of this publication, visit our{' '}
      <a href="/doctrinal-basis/">Doctrinal Basis</a>, browse the <a href="/glossary/">Site Glossary</a>, or write to our desk directly
      through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
